            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "The price of a new boat is $28 000. It depreciates by 20% of its value each year.",
              "marks": []
            },
            {
              "type": "break"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Find how long it will take for the boat to depreciate to $11000. Answer to the nearest year.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "id": "p26-q11-bank-p26-q11-trial-hint",
          "type": "paragraph",
          "fontSize": null,
          "align": "left",
          "spaceBefore": 0,
          "spaceAfter": 1,
          "lineHeight": 1.4,
          "indent": 0,
          "inlines": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "text": "Hint: set up the compound depreciation equation and use trial and error to estimate n. Refine your trials around the target, then round the estimated time as requested.",
              "marks": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "4 years",
      "worked": "$$11000=28000(0.8)^n$$\nUse trial and error:\n$$\\begin{align*}S(4)&=28000(0.8)^4=\\$11\\,468.80\\\\S(4.2)&=28000(0.8)^{4.2}\\approx\\$10\\,968.22\\end{align*}$$\nThe target is reached between 4 and 4.2 years, so the time is 4 years to the nearest year.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 40
  },
